  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=2{e}^{t}\\,i+\\sqrt{t+4}\\,j+(t-2)^{4}\\,k$ at $t=0?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =2{e}^{0}\\,i+\\sqrt{0+4}\\,j+(0-2)^{4}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=0$ is the vector $2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k.$",
